ition":{"commit_sha":"004552a9cc10269f5dcd4835e3175d52e9228435","position":"1787022989129321001-94a24b71-e082-46bf-934d-7c5c18a2eef7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"36e4ffe6d8187e9e2b6b3b9be6fa80dbc0d6bca2ff4b2cb48205775d79d77597","event_uuid":"502d320b-0ead-44ab-b3db-e1825d69555b","position":{"commit_sha":"97849c989c7245ee4f2802a20de852e0dc69817b","position":"1787023063347901001-502d320b-0ead-44ab-b3db-e1825d69555b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ec10e575f7666d4feefa58e63135db81f64651d9a2e5d94a2cbeda64c3913eb6","event_uuid":"063b3f02-341b-4429-94ef-4722b27dd48b","position":{"commit_sha":"d815e0cff6f5555726ed4e042cc9b915d18fcb38","position":"1787023202940268001-063b3f02-341b-4429-94ef-4722b27dd48b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787022424824041001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`binding_store.py` is at the 800-line hard boundary because file loading, unknown-field preservation, tempfile cleanup, JSON encoding, GET-rotation ordering, retired-state replacement, and alert persistence live beside identity policy. Moving those branches without direct byte/fault oracles could turn known recoverable partial states into silent data loss.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract a private `BindingRepository`/unit-of-work behind the unchanged public `BindingStore` facade. The repository owns paths and the original dictionaries, returns open typed views over those same dictionaries, and preserves every existing load/save byte and exception contract. `peer_state.py` and `get_rotation.py` remain independent owners. Record the internal ownership and recovery/cutover constraints in the binding-lifecycle ADR.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a cohesive repository module for live, retired, rotation, and alert paths; current load/corruption rules; JSON tempfiles; per-file `os.replace`; and dirty/change gating. Do not introduce a multi-file atomicity claim.\n2. Move persistence calls behind facade delegates without changing `BindingStore` construction, loader, public signatures, shared inner dictionaries, or caller-visible exceptions.\n3. Preserve rotation-before-live order and the inline rotation floor, retired-first move ordering, best-effort alert writes, and exact sorted/indented/newline serialization.\n4. Keep tickets publication in `reconcile_helpers.py` as an external five-file allowlisted seam. Add no broad staging and no publish at each local checkpoint.\n5. Add an ADR that distinguishes repository unit-of-work durability from tickets publication and records the later exact-match recovery boundary.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- A direct-repository suite loads legacy/unknown-field fixtures and asserts byte-equal round trips and no eager rewrite.\n- Failure cuts inject tempfile, rotation replace, retired replace, live replace, alert write, and selective commit failures. Oracles are exact surviving files/bytes, raised versus swallowed outcome, alert/tally, and unchanged HEAD where applicable.\n- Public-facade regressions assert pending/confirmed/reverse lookup and the current shallow `all_bindings()` compatibility.\n- Existing GET-rotation and selective-publication suites remain the cross-seam oracle.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nThis is an internal delegation only. Reverting the facade delegation restores the previous implementation over identical files. No format migration, eager rewrite, public import change, deep copy, general journal, or `git add -A` is permitted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given legacy records and unknown fields, direct repository and public-facade load/save preserve semantic fields and exact sorted/indented/trailing-newline bytes without an eager write.\n- [ ] Given each named fault cut, tests observe the documented old/new file combination and the same raise/swallow/alert behavior as before extraction.\n- [ ] GET rotation is durably attempted before live replacement; a failed sidecar save retains the newest inline floor and a later retry converges.\n- [ ] `BindingStore` import, constructor, loader, signatures, shared inner-entry behavior, and existing peer/get-rotation delegates remain compatible.\n- [ ] Tickets publication still stages only the existing five bridge-state files and an unchanged pass creates no commit.\n- [ ] The ADR states repository ownership, ordered partial-state behavior, selective publication, rollback, and the no-journal/no-format-migration decision.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_repository.py","reason":"New byte-preserving persistence and unit-of-work owner."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Delegate persistence behind the compatible facade."},{"path":"docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md","reason":"Record repository/lifecycle/recovery ownership and durability choices."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Index the binding-store ADR."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py","reason":"Direct byte, corruption, and fault-cut repository oracles."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_store.py","reason":"Facade compatibility and save/reload regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py","reason":"Rotation-before-live and failure-floor regression adjustments."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_retired_commit.py","reason":"Selective retirement publication regression adjustments."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp02","reconciler","persistence","tdd"],"ticket_id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-02 S1 — Extract the byte-preserving binding repository","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_store.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_corrupt_state_guard.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Direct repository bytes, facade compatibility, corruption, and rotation fault cuts"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_retired_commit.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_commit_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_commit_binding_store_failure.py","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"Five-file selective publication and unchanged-pass idempotency"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"ADR numbering and documentation index integrity"}]